    "body": "## Chat05A follow-up: authored-text trigger is blocked by TWO authoritative contracts (2026-10-30)\n\nRead-only crosscheck on exact PR HEAD `463d75ae9181fae886ae9e198698219f95106993` and current main `b435e70eb88b87b3c3324ef2a2da14cdf473f229`, Chat01 `PASS_SPEC`, canonical Notion memory `2026-10-30-CHAT03-EXTERNAL-SECRETS-OPTION-RESEARCH-R230`, plan V15.\n\nCurrent DRAW-only implementation and its local tests are not being rejected. **Chat05A overall PASS remains blocked** for these concrete reasons:\n\n1. **Trusted edited-text provenance is absent.** The Worker accepts tactical selections with exactly five fields (`attackColor/defenseColor/attackType/defenseType/role`); no server-authored canonical ready-phrase source or committed final edited text exists in the battle snapshot. Client-supplied `nextTextOrigin`, `previousAuthoredText`, `hasEdited`, phrase IDs unbound to the server, or a browser boolean must not be treated as authoritative. The server must know the reference ready text and the final confirmed text/provenance, bound to the same battle, participant, and immutable commitment. ↻ ready-phrase refresh, opening/cancelling edit, or punctuation/case/spacing-only changes are no-trigger. Changing words and then returning to the original is no-trigger. The Word/Unicode normalization should be checked against the Chat01 spec, not only simple punctuation stripping.\n\n2. **Existing lifecycle + DB explicitly assume DRAW-only voting.** Current `AsyncScene/Web/conflict/tactical-lifecycle.js` `validateState()` requires `socialOutcome=NONE` for a revealed non-DRAW, while Chat01 mandates `PENDING` when a real edited-text vote opens; `gameplay-server/migrations/0008_chat05a_people_and_votes.sql` checks `trigger_reason = 'DRAW'` and its vote-creation gate checks `mechanicalOutcome = 'DRAW'`. Simply adding an API text flag or a `social_votes` row would produce inconsistent authoritative lifecycle state/DB constraints.\n\n**Next narrow atom:** First design/test the minimal server-owned canonical ready-text/reference + final-author-text commit contract, including what happens for both A and B, legacy textless battles, retries, reload, and a non-DRAW reveal. Map the exact lifecycle and D1 invariants and migration changes before coding. Then make the smallest coordinated change on the SAME Chat05A branch/PR only after fresh shared-file ownership/locks and source/deployed mirror checks. Keep `mechanicalOutcome` immutable, one `voteId` per battle, and existing authorized DRAW votes/receipts intact. No Chat05B, NPC, close/deadline/economy, Cloudflare migration/deploy, main write or merge. Require exact-HEAD CI, local Worker/D1 negative/replay/concurrency/restart coverage, and independent critical security/persistence review before claiming Chat05A PASS.\n\nThis is a coordination/review note, not an implementation or a new PASS.",
